# The only required environment variable. Every other runtime setting (base URL, authentication
# secret, OAuth credentials, email delivery, API keys, legal links) is stored in the database
# `config` table and managed in the browser at /configure, where the operator signs in with the
# username and password from this connection string.
# Local development defaults come from .env.development; shell variables always win, and
# mode-specific local overrides belong in .env.development.local.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Email via SES: set the region and (optionally) a static access-key pair at /configure. When the
# credential fields are left unset there, the AWS SDK credential chain (role, SSO, or profile) of
# the deployment is used instead.
# AWS_PROFILE=
